Nested Loops Challenge 🤔
Problem: How to implement nested loops?

for (int i = 100; i != 0; i--)
    for (int j = 50; j != 0; j--)
        // inner loop body


Challenge: LOOP instruction uses only ONE counter (ECX)!


Solution: Save and restore the outer loop counter

Simple IF Statement
C++ Code:
if (x &gt; 2000)
    x = x / 2;

Switch Statement
C++ Code:
switch (x) {
case 0:  y = 1;   break;
case 2:  y = 10;  break; 
case 4:  y = 100; break;
default: y = 0;
}

WHILE Loop Translation
C++ Code:
d1 = 100; d2 = 0; t = 0;
while (d2 &lt;= d1) {
    t = t + 1;
    d1 = d1 - 3;
    d2 = 2*t - 1;
}
